#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""epterm - print your terminal to a 4.2" Waveshare e-Paper (V2).

Sources (all stream into the same display):
  * stdin        some_command | epterm          (one-shot or streaming)
  * named pipe   epterm --pipe                  then: echo hi > /tmp/epterm
  * tmux         epterm --tmux [SECS]           mirror the active tmux pane
  * keyboard     epterm --shell [DEVICE]        a real interactive bash shell
                                                 driven by a USB keyboard and
                                                 rendered via a VT100 emulator

The last ~rows lines are drawn in a monospace font on the 400x300 panel.
The first frame is a full refresh; later frames use flicker-free partial
refresh with a full refresh every N updates to avoid ghosting. The panel
powers off when idle and after every session.
"""
